{"id":"H6855","lemma":"צִפֹּרָה","transliteration":"tsipporah","sayIt":"tsip-po-RAH","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Zipporah","meaning":"A woman living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Exo.2.21;\ndaughter of: Jethro (H3503);\nsister of: Eliasaph (H0460) and Hobab (H2246); married to Moses (H4872);\nmother of: Gershom (H1647) and Eliezer (H0461H)\n§ Zipporah = \"bird\"\ndaughter of Reuel or Jethro, wife of Moses, and mother of Gershom and Eliezer","glosses":["zipporah"],"count":3,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"exo-2","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"Zipporah","kjv":"Zipporah"}},{"chapterId":"exo-4","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"But Zipporah","kjv":"Then Zipporah"}},{"chapterId":"exo-18","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"Zipporah","kjv":"Zipporah"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Exodus 2:21","note":"Moses was content to dwell with the man. He gave Moses Zipporah, his daughter.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H0460","lemma":"אֶלְיָסָף","transliteration":"elyasaph","gloss":"Eliasaph"},{"id":"H0461","lemma":"אֱלִיעֶ֫זֶר","transliteration":"eliezer","gloss":"Eliezer"},{"id":"H1647","lemma":"גֵּרְשֹׁם","transliteration":"gereshom","gloss":"Gershom"},{"id":"H2246","lemma":"חֹבָב","transliteration":"chovav","gloss":"Hobab"},{"id":"H3503","lemma":"יִתְרוֹ","transliteration":"yitro","gloss":"Jethro"},{"id":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","transliteration":"mosheh","gloss":"Moses"},{"id":"H3500","lemma":"יֶ֫תֶר","transliteration":"yeter","gloss":"Jether"},{"id":"H4519","lemma":"מְנַשֶּׁה","transliteration":"menashsheh","gloss":"Manasseh"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}